# H264.qsf -- Quartus 17.0.2 project for the MiSTer H264 core.
#
# THE FILE LIST BELOW GATES MORE THAN THE COMPILE. tools/lint_undriven.sh lints exactly
# the files named here, and tools/netlist_canary.sh reads the map report this project
# writes. A new h264/*.sv that is not named here is invisible to Quartus AND to both
# gates: the compile fails on an undefined entity, or worse, elaborates without it.
# Add the SYSTEMVERILOG_FILE line in the same commit as the module.
#
# Do NOT hand-edit the pin/HPS assignments: they come from `source sys/sys.tcl` and
# `source sys/sys_analog.tcl`, which Quartus expands into this file on open. If it
# writes the expansion back, revert it (build_release.sh restores a rewritten qsf;
# tools/seed_sweep.sh restores its own snapshot).
#
# SEED LEDGER (append one line per fit that ships or teaches something; never delete):
#   date (branch/slug): SEED n, clk_dec 100C/-40C MHz, ALM %, M10K, DSP, build name, commit
#   -- the fitter SEED is tied to the EXACT synthesis netlist. ANY change to the
#      netlist, including a CONF_STR row or the CORE_VERSION string, re-rolls it.
#      tools/seed_sweep.sh finds a passing seed; tools/fmax_check.sh gates BOTH corners.
